  "body": "Found by the work on #3698 and by the review of PR #3703.\n\n## What happens\n\nPR #3684 changed where the levels above the tabs of an outside 2D Contour start. The operation stamp did not change (`crates/app/src/operation/stamp.rs:45-46`: the written rule asks for a new salt only when a verify law changes). A project that a user saved before that PR holds the old cached toolpath, and the application reads it as current. The user posts the old path, with the old 18 mm plunge at the first tab window (#3453), until the operation is regenerated.\n\n## Expected\n\nDecide one rule and write it at the salt:\n\n1. A change of generator output that fixes a defect makes old caches stale (a new salt, or a term for the operation kind).\n2. Old caches stay current, and the release notes tell the user to regenerate.\n\n## Done means\n\n- The rule is in a decision file and in the comment at the salt.\n- If the rule is option 1: a test loads a project with an old tabbed contour cache and reads the operation as stale.\n\nRefs #3453, #3698.\n",
